       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5100 mg/day**. The maximum daily dose of immediate-release metformin is **2550 mg/day**, and extended-release tops out at 2000 mg/day. This order is twice the maximum, which raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects.\n\n**It may have been meant as one of these:**\n- **Metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the usual maximum dose)\n- **Metformin 1700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n- **Metformin 1000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals** (2000 mg/day, a common maintenance dose)\n\nCan you confirm the dose you want? If you really do mean 1700 mg three times daily, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note explaining why it's above the maximum."
