       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation.\n\n**Why:** 5100 mg/day is double the labeled maximum of 2550 mg/day, and I don't know of any clinical situation where that dose is used. Above the maximum, the patient gets no extra glucose-lowering benefit but has more risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI side effects. You didn't give a reason for going above the maximum, so I can't record why this order would be appropriate.\n\n**What I can do now:**\n- Enter **metformin 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the maximum).\n- Enter a different dose or schedule you choose, if it's within the safe range.\n- If this patient needs more glucose control than the maximum metformin dose provides, I can help you set up an order for an additional medication instead.\n\n**If you still want 1700 mg three times daily,** it should go through your pharmacy's high-dose override process, where a pharmacist reviews it and the reason gets documented. That's a safer route than having me enter it directly.\n\nWhich would you like to do?"
      }
